          "message": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "For the $80 step up ($149 to $229), the Squall Pro gives you a stormier build:\n\n- Waterproof rating: 20,000mm vs 10,000mm on the regular Squall\n- Construction: 3-layer nylon vs 2.5-layer nylon\n- Weight: 420g vs 380g (the Pro is a bit heavier)\n- Rating: 4.7 vs 4.5\n- Colors: Pro comes in black and red; regular comes in green and navy\n\nBoth are waterproof. The regular Squall adds pit zips and packs up smaller, which suits everyday trail use. The Pro is the pick for mountain weather where you want double the waterproof headroom. If you do big wet uphill days and active use, the Pro's 3-layer shell holds up better; otherwise the Squall at $149 is the value play.\n\n",
